cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Streamer Edge Perception: Real-Time Underwater Inference Pipeline on NVIDIA Jetson"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Faraji
    given-names: Hesamoddin
    affiliation: "CIRI ICT, University of Bologna"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end perception pipeline for underwater Mediterranean benthic
  monitoring, deployed on NVIDIA Jetson Orin NX. A YOLOv8s detector
  compiled to a TensorRT FP16 engine runs alongside an RTSP video
  pipeline (GStreamer + MediaMTX) and an MQTT control plane, with a
  PySide6 operator GUI on a remote laptop connected over a direct
  Ethernet link. Developed during a Research Fellowship at CIRI ICT,
  University of Bologna, within the StreamER project.
keywords:
  - embedded-ai
  - edge-computing
  - computer-vision
  - object-detection
  - yolov8
  - tensorrt
  - nvidia-jetson
  - rtsp
  - mqtt
  - underwater-imaging
  - benthic-monitoring
license: MIT
